  <text>
    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="2.1">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IAtr">I Atr</ref> 2.1</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="2.1" corresp="#wit-h">⁊ æt ðam oðrum cyrre ne sy þær nan oþer bot buton þæt heafod.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="2.1" corresp="#wit-b">⁊ æt ðam oðran cyrre ne sy ðær nan bót buton þæt heafod.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="2.1" corresp="#wit-q">Ad secundam uicem non sit illic alia emendatio quam capitalis.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="2.1" corresp="#wit-b">⁊ æt ðam oðran cyrre ne sy ðær nan bót buton þæt heafod.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann">Und beim zweiten Male gebe es da keine andere Busse als den Kopf.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And the second time let there be no other compensation there than the head.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-b">And on the second occasion he shall not be able to make any amends except by his head.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="221"><ref target="clause:IAtr_1-6">I Atr 1.6</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">Vgl. 1, 6</note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#liebermann"><ref target="clause:IICn_32-1">II Cn 32.1</ref></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#whitelock" n="467"><ref target="clause:IICn_32">II Cn 32</ref></note>
        <note type="editorial">Liebermann compares I Atr 1.6.</note>
      </div>
    </body>
